From: Droidloom development build
Subject: [PATCH] EGL: a multi-file cache entry fits any buffer large enough for it

get() checked that the caller's buffer holds the entry, then required the
buffer to be exactly the entry's size. Mesa asks with a 64 KiB buffer, so
every shader it had stored read as a mismatch and was compiled again.
---
--- a/opengl/libs/EGL/MultifileBlobCache.cpp
+++ b/opengl/libs/EGL/MultifileBlobCache.cpp
@@ -513,9 +513,10 @@
         cacheEntry = mHotCache[entryHash].entryBuffer;
     }
 
-    // Ensure the header matches
+    // Ensure the header matches. valueSize is the caller's buffer, which may
+    // be larger than the entry; the entry's own size is cachedValueSize.
     MultifileHeader* header = reinterpret_cast<MultifileHeader*>(cacheEntry);
-    if (header->keySize != keySize || header->valueSize != valueSize) {
+    if (header->keySize != keySize || header->valueSize != cachedValueSize) {
         ALOGW("Mismatch on keySize(%ld vs. cached %ld) or valueSize(%ld vs. cached %ld) compared "
               "to cache header values for fullPath: %s",
               keySize, header->keySize, valueSize, header->valueSize, fullPath.c_str());
